{* ROTARY — orders · claims · helper *}
<div class="rt-prose rt-helper-copy">
<div align="justify">An insurance claim is a formal request by a policyholder to an insurance company for coverage or compensation for a covered loss or policy event. The insurance company validates the claim (or denies the claim). <br /><br />If it is approved, the insurance company will issue payment to the insured or an approved interested party on behalf of the insured.<br /><br />
Generally, a beneficiary can apply for the proceeds simply by filling out the  claim form here and submitting it to the company along with a certified copy of the death certificate.<br /><br />
<div align="center"><b class="rt-strong rt-tone-royal">ADDITIONAL INFORMATION</b></div>
After a loved one dies, beneficiaries need to know how to collect life insurance and Social Security payments they're entitled to, because the executor of the estate doesn't usually handle this task.<br /><br />Especially if survivors depended on the deceased person for financial support, they may need to quickly get cash for urgent, ongoing expenses such as the mortgage, school fees and credit card payments.<br /><br />
{Msgs::Warning('For more information, please email us on <a rel="mailto:[[CE]]">[[CE]]</a> or call us on <b>[[CP]]</b>')}
</div>
